{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/85186-thoughts-in-a-restless-slumber","id":85186,"title":"Thoughts in a restless slumber.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-06T01:49:55-08:00","id":85186,"title":"Thoughts in a restless slumber.","content":"I'm torn. Literally. Figuratively. Spiritually. Why couldn't I have just accepted my fate. I was young, foolish, naive. Ugh, I was eager. Too eager for my own good. I was too young, and it was only my first death. This is now my third. I know what is about to happen, the sun will soon rise, and so too shall I. This knowledge and experience doesn't make it any easier. The Fanged Skull is away, but soon he will show me the cost of my continued existence. I pray this time it's someone who deserves it. Probably not. I'm not so fortunate. He may have let me avenge my murder, but that pales in the sins I must eat, shoved down my throat by this... I hate him! <br /> <br /> Great, I can feel his cackle on the back of my neck. The sun must be cresting. Ugh! OH man, I hate that part. Being pulled back out of the gateway. It always seems like a piece of me is ripped off and left behind. I can feel the caul on my face. I squeeze my eyes tighter, but it won't help; I will still be forced to see. It's through his eyes the vision comes. <br /> <br /> The living room was dim, only the glow of a television illuminated the family. Sitting so happily, laughing at the sitcom, eating dinner off of food tray stands. A father, a mother, two boys and a teenage girl. My heart drops. I know this family. My half-brother sits there, unaware of the horror I loosed into his life. Non of these are acceptable. I try to scream. &quot;JUST LEAVE ME DEAD!&quot; I feel the pain of such forceful yelling deep in my throat, hear nothing. I only ever hear the screams of the victim. The Fanged Skull is standing behind my family now. I can see they are watching some sitcom about office working. My brother looks to be laughing heartily. Leaning in, I see that he is whispering into the my sister-in-law's ear. Her laughter stops. She picks up the steak knife, gingerly wipes it off with her napkin, moves her tray to the side. She saddles up to her husband, nuzzles the side of his neck, and draws the knife across his throat. The kids are laughing too hard, they mistake the gargled cough as nothing at first.<br /> <br /> Oh god, why does it have to be in front of the children? God? HA! What kind of god lets this happen? No! I must not doubt! I must hold faith in something if I am to keep myself through this again!<br /> <br /> The pain in my throat is far more real this time. The harsh cold morning air stings from the lips all the way to the bottom of my lungs. I gasp in the first breath of my fourth life, a life stolen from a father, a family man. A man who's home was filled with pictures of him and his smiling family. His ghost ripped through the same gate meant for me. He's in the underworld now. Before his time. And I am here, breathing, heart pounding. Alive. I'm alive. He's dead. Murdered by his wife. All because The Fanged Mask needed someone's death to take my place as he brings me back. Again. And again. And again.<br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> I had to post a short, due to all of the mislead conceptions of what a Geist game is. Full of hope my arse! This happens EVERY time the Sin-Eater is brought back by the Geist. And the Sin-Eater is forced to see it, witness it in full, EVERY time. <br /> <br /> And this is why I love Geist as a Story Telling game. It's part of the World of Darkness. Not the World of Dimness. Not the World of Slightly Morbid I died but got Better so Everything Will be Okay Now. Read some gothic literature sometime. I was kind, and left the children to your own imagination, and did not use them for more than ambiance in the setting. <br /> <br /> Now, with this in mind, go back and really look at Geist: The Sin-Eaters. Sure, it can have fun moments, light hearted moments, it can even have hope, and achieve good and positive things. But there's always this thing in them. This aberrant minded alien being that is a mixture of ghost and spirit. It wants your body so it can enjoy the material world. It is riding you! You are nothing but a tool to it. Not the most obedient tool, but a tool. In the eyes of a werewolf, you are a Ridden, an abomination to be destroyed. In fact, Sin-Eaters are worse than the Ridden. You're a Magoth Ridden. Abomination to Spirits and Werewolves alike. <br /> <br /> You are not a lucky sod brought back by a benevolent Caspar wannabe. STOP IT! Learn words. Terrible is a word. Horrific is a word. They both apply to the condition of being returned as a Sin-Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1033-lathcon","name":"Lathcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1033_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T02:47:51-08:00","id":85204,"title":"","content":"Relax dude. Easy, easy. Speaking of easy, it would very easy just to say &quot;Geist is a storyteller system. That story is what you make of it, and while your story might be morbid to the point of being disgusting, mine dosen't nessesarily have to have any of that.&quot;. But since its so easy, I wont go with that.<br /> <br /> No, instead, I'll tell you, you're compleatly right. Geist is a game of morbid nihillism and brutal death thrust upon an unwanting little insignificant speck of a person, by an unfeeling unliving abominable god of death. And its also about the crazy drug fueled parties, the cryptic Twillight Network, the philosophy, the sex, the drink and fun!<br /> <br /> Geist is very much a game of contrasts, and to me, thats what makes it awesome. Its a very solid parody/mirror of life. Life isn't all fairy dust and rose scented farts, but it isn't all death, gloom and darkness either. Its an unwholesom mix of the two, married in an imperfect harmony that any moment threatens to tip an either direction, unbalancing the whole thing for a bloody moment, before harmony eventually reassrts itself for those who still live.<br /> <br /> And as a Sin-Eater, that &quot;Who still live&quot; will inevitably be you. So while it has its dark moment, i feel like Geist: The Sin-Eaters stands out amongst the other titles, as the game that recognises that more light-hearted side of life. The joy and the dance. Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling and Promethean all have grim-dark shit going on, but neither really acknowledges that life is also a happy place filled with laugher and merry. Geist does.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nice short story, btw. Nicely written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T03:12:16-08:00","id":85209,"title":"","content":"Thank you Krobeles. And yes I do agree with you. You very nicely expanded on a point that I merely skimmed over and didn't give a second thought to in the post. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lathcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/85186-thoughts-in-a-restless-slumber#post85186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, with this in mind, go back and really look at Geist: The Sin-Eaters. Sure, it can have fun moments, light hearted moments, it can even have hope, and achieve good and positive things. But there's always this thing in them...</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first Geist games I played in, my friend played a druggy who died of an overdose, and contributed everything Geisty to being part of a trip as he continued to drug out. It led to many laughs and light hearted moments in the mix as well. <br /> <br /> Making a direct point towards the other games also brings about a slight reworking of my opinion, as in the VtR: Blood and Smoke game I'm running right now has it's dark moments, the players staying true to their characters find ways to have a happy moment whenever they can (and yes, I do let them have it. I'm not all Kali Ma). I guess I was just feeling especially cruel tonight. Also, after writing a short like that, a little hard to go jovial in an explanation for it. <br /> <br /> Next time I write something dark, I'm taking a snack break and watching a sitcom before I expand on any of the W's. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1033-lathcon","name":"Lathcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1033_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}